    "body": "On 5/13/2020 10:17 PM, Anne van Kesteren wrote:\n> Wouldn't `table.caption.textContent` be a better way to go? Your code assumes that it contains a single child, which may not be true.\n> \n\nWow! In over ten years, off and on, of reading the\nstandard, I had never encountered textContent. It\nis not a global attribute, and looking at the element\ndescriptions it is not even listed as an attribute\noutside the global attributes.\n\n\n    Why not?\n\n\nFollowing the links to the DOM standard, which I don't\nlook at so regularly, textContent is there, but pretty obscure.\n\n\nWell, this changes a lot; I'll have to do some tests\nand experiments and likely revise a lot of my\nlectures.\n\n\nThanks for the lead, sorry I hadn't seen that a long\ntime ago.\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n-Steve\n",
