    "body": "We're entering Stack Overflow territory, but roughly, elements in HTML map to classes, which are called interfaces in IDL. Confusingly, both elements and interfaces have things called attributes. While they often seem similar, e.g., `lang=\"\"` and `.lang`, they are distinct and defined independently. `textContent` is an attribute/property that only exists on an interface. I.e., you cannot write `<html textContent=\"...\">` and therefore it is not a global attribute (those are attributes for elements). Hope that helps.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
